1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,875
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,416 --> 00:00:06,208
Recognize
this banner mount, Zanth?

3
00:00:06,208 --> 00:00:07,875
I wielded one just like it

4
00:00:07,875 --> 00:00:10,625
when we rode into
the Battle of Two Skies.

5
00:00:10,625 --> 00:00:12,458
[grumbling roar]

6
00:00:12,458 --> 00:00:14,083
[chuckling]

7
00:00:14,083 --> 00:00:16,541
So, I'm glad to have guests.

8
00:00:16,541 --> 00:00:17,750
Tea?

9
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:18,958
Actually, Arrakore,

10
00:00:18,958 --> 00:00:21,333
we have to get to a place
called the Cave of Tones

11
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:22,291
and wake a dragon,

12
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:24,416
or, like, half a dragon?

13
00:00:24,416 --> 00:00:26,708
We don't know if it's
the front half or the back half.

14
00:00:26,708 --> 00:00:28,375
Aw, Sora, please.

15
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:30,583
You'd only need to wake
the Arc Dragon

16
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:33,500
if you were going up against
the Shatter Dragon of Chaos,

17
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,583
which, I mean... [laughing]

18
00:00:35,583 --> 00:00:37,500
good luck if that ever happens,

19
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,375
b-because--

20
00:00:39,375 --> 00:00:40,541
Oh.

21
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:41,541
For real?

22
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,541
You're fighting ThunderFang?

23
00:00:43,541 --> 00:00:45,166
Well, that's tough,

24
00:00:45,166 --> 00:00:48,208
Oh, but at least he didn't die
and go to the Spectral Lands,

25
00:00:48,208 --> 00:00:50,875
where his power could...
[chuckling]

26
00:00:50,875 --> 00:00:52,208
[grumbling sadly]

27
00:00:52,208 --> 00:00:54,000
Oh, he did?

28
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,291
Well, you know...

29
00:00:56,291 --> 00:00:59,375
good luck anyway, I guess?

30
00:00:59,375 --> 00:01:01,541
Please tell me you've restored
enough of Djinjago

31
00:01:01,541 --> 00:01:03,291
that the Cave of Tones is back.

32
00:01:03,291 --> 00:01:04,458
[Arrakore] I sure have.

33
00:01:04,458 --> 00:01:06,666
Right there,

34
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:09,208
but there's
no half-dragon in it.

35
00:01:09,208 --> 00:01:10,208
[groaning] Ugh!

36
00:01:10,208 --> 00:01:11,250
Why not?

37
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:14,250
My wish magic isn't yet
strong enough

38
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:15,833
to bring back living things,

39
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:17,541
like the Arc Dragon,

40
00:01:17,541 --> 00:01:19,208
or my people,

41
00:01:19,208 --> 00:01:20,333
so I've had to settle

42
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:22,916
for reviving
our cultural artifacts.

43
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,083
The upside?

44
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:27,250
I've brought back
some really excellent pottery.

45
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:29,208
The workmanship!

46
00:01:31,208 --> 00:01:33,625
Delilah doesn't like
to be moved!

47
00:01:33,625 --> 00:01:35,208
I told you,

48
00:01:35,208 --> 00:01:36,875
it gets pretty lonely.

49
00:01:36,875 --> 00:01:38,875
Maybe all your magic needs

50
00:01:38,875 --> 00:01:40,458
is the right motivation,

51
00:01:40,458 --> 00:01:42,250
like saving the world.

52
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:43,875
Arrakore, I wish

53
00:01:43,875 --> 00:01:46,458
for the Arc Dragon of Focus
to be restored.

54
00:01:47,458 --> 00:01:48,958
[breathing deeply]

55
00:01:48,958 --> 00:01:52,541
Your wish is yours to keep...

56
00:01:52,541 --> 00:01:54,500
maybe.

57
00:01:56,041 --> 00:02:00,333
Actually, with Zanth's
new boost of Djinjagan magic,

58
00:02:00,333 --> 00:02:02,083
we might have enough power...

59
00:02:02,083 --> 00:02:04,541
if we work together.

60
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:05,666
[grumbling roar]

61
00:02:05,666 --> 00:02:07,333
A wish of this magnitude

62
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:10,500
will take time
and complete concentration.

63
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,083
That means no distractions.

64
00:02:12,083 --> 00:02:15,000
Even loud noises
could destroy our focus

65
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,208
and ruin the wish.

66
00:02:16,208 --> 00:02:17,625
The world hangs in the balance,

67
00:02:17,625 --> 00:02:19,583
so you won't hear a peep
from us.

68
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:21,833
We're Ninja.
Stealth is our thing.

69
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:27,833
[metal clanking]

70
00:02:27,833 --> 00:02:29,541
These metal shoes
are not comfortable,

71
00:02:29,541 --> 00:02:31,625
but I like the noise they make!

72
00:02:31,625 --> 00:02:32,541
Clang! Clang!

73
00:02:32,541 --> 00:02:34,208
[clanking]

74
00:02:34,208 --> 00:02:35,166
What?

75
00:02:35,166 --> 00:02:36,208
Did I miss something?

76
00:02:36,208 --> 00:02:39,250
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

77
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:42,416
♪ Together we will rise ♪

78
00:02:42,416 --> 00:02:45,875
♪ We fight ♪

79
00:02:45,875 --> 00:02:49,000
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

80
00:02:50,166 --> 00:02:51,166
[thunderclap]

81
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:53,708
Aah!

82
00:02:53,708 --> 00:02:56,083
[gasping for breath]

83
00:02:56,083 --> 00:02:57,208
[groaning]

84
00:02:57,208 --> 00:02:58,958
[Ras] Leaving you alone,

85
00:02:58,958 --> 00:03:00,208
defenseless,

86
00:03:00,208 --> 00:03:03,083
gone on more important business.

87
00:03:03,083 --> 00:03:04,875
Does it hurt to realize

88
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:07,500
the Ninja
care so little for you?

89
00:03:08,791 --> 00:03:12,458
[Sora and Frak]
♪ Da-da-da-da-da... ♪

90
00:03:12,458 --> 00:03:15,916
No, it-it's... ♪ Da-da ♪

91
00:03:15,916 --> 00:03:16,958
[grumbling]

92
00:03:16,958 --> 00:03:19,000
It-it's... ♪ Da-Da ♪

93
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,125
You go--you go up after.

94
00:03:20,125 --> 00:03:22,250
♪ Bum-ba-ba-bum-bum
Bum-bum! ♪

95
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:23,583
Shush!

96
00:03:23,583 --> 00:03:25,416
[whispering] Oh, right.

97
00:03:25,416 --> 00:03:28,125
How are we supposed
to remember this boring song

98
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:30,250
if we can't make any noise?

99
00:03:31,291 --> 00:03:34,583
[novelty car horn
blaring "La Cucaracha"]

100
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:36,125
No, you're way off.

101
00:03:36,125 --> 00:03:37,916
That wasn't me.

102
00:03:37,916 --> 00:03:40,583
[novelty car horn blaring]

103
00:03:46,875 --> 00:03:48,458
Rapton lives!

104
00:03:48,458 --> 00:03:49,791
Shh!

105
00:03:49,791 --> 00:03:51,166
Shushing Rapton?

106
00:03:51,166 --> 00:03:52,166
How rude!

107
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:53,833
What are you goons doing here?

108
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:55,333
Thievin'.

109
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:56,833
All this Djinjago loot

110
00:03:56,833 --> 00:04:00,416
is Djinja-going
home with us! Heh.

111
00:04:00,416 --> 00:04:02,000
So, why are we whispering?

112
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,083
Because... these relics
belong to a powerful Djinn

113
00:04:05,083 --> 00:04:07,000
asleep in that cave.

114
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,166
He'll be real angry
if he wakes up.

115
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:10,708
Huh, okay,

116
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:14,541
an angry Djinn would cut into
Rapton's profit margin.

117
00:04:14,541 --> 00:04:15,375
[sighing]

118
00:04:15,375 --> 00:04:16,958
Freebooters,

119
00:04:16,958 --> 00:04:20,041
spread out and grab
all the treasure you can,

120
00:04:20,041 --> 00:04:21,416
quiet-like,

121
00:04:21,416 --> 00:04:22,458
but remember,

122
00:04:22,458 --> 00:04:24,291
if you find that jeweled box,

123
00:04:24,291 --> 00:04:25,875
it belongs to me.

124
00:04:25,875 --> 00:04:27,375
We can't let you
steal this stuff.

125
00:04:27,375 --> 00:04:29,083
There's time to fight.

126
00:04:29,083 --> 00:04:30,250
[powering weapons]

127
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:31,708
What about noise?

128
00:04:31,708 --> 00:04:33,416
[scoffing] Everyone knows

129
00:04:33,416 --> 00:04:37,541
Rapton is a Mighty
Combat Panther of Stealth!

130
00:04:37,541 --> 00:04:38,375
[groaning with impact]

131
00:04:38,375 --> 00:04:40,333
[whispering] Attack!

132
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:41,333
[gasping]

133
00:04:41,333 --> 00:04:42,333
[boulder thudding]

134
00:04:42,333 --> 00:04:45,125
No gem-stealing, nin-joker!

135
00:04:46,583 --> 00:04:48,000
Hold up, big guy. We--

136
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,125
[clearing throat]

137
00:04:49,125 --> 00:04:51,791
...I mean, I...

138
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:54,458
I don't want your gems,

139
00:04:54,458 --> 00:04:56,333
because it's just me.

140
00:04:56,333 --> 00:04:59,458
I just need into the cave
behind there

141
00:04:59,458 --> 00:05:00,541
to ring bells,

142
00:05:00,541 --> 00:05:03,791
or else the world
will be destroyed.

143
00:05:03,791 --> 00:05:06,125
World destroyed?

144
00:05:06,125 --> 00:05:07,958
But PowerLid needs world!

145
00:05:07,958 --> 00:05:10,708
That's where PowerLid
keeps his gems!

146
00:05:10,708 --> 00:05:12,083
Oh, no!

147
00:05:12,083 --> 00:05:14,750
PowerLid just said out loud
where he keeps gems.

148
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:16,208
Anyone could've heard.

149
00:05:16,208 --> 00:05:18,541
Security risk!

150
00:05:18,541 --> 00:05:22,208
Uh... okay,
so I'll just go in.

151
00:05:22,208 --> 00:05:23,583
Yes, little bi-clops,

152
00:05:23,583 --> 00:05:24,875
you go save world.

153
00:05:24,875 --> 00:05:26,458
Only cost you four gems.

154
00:05:26,458 --> 00:05:28,000
You're charging me?

155
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,333
To save the world?

156
00:05:30,333 --> 00:05:32,208
I demand you let me pass!

157
00:05:32,208 --> 00:05:33,416
"Demand"?

158
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:34,333
Great!

159
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:36,541
Now cost eight gems!

160
00:05:36,541 --> 00:05:40,333
PowerLid practice surge pricing
at times of peak demand.

161
00:05:40,333 --> 00:05:42,458
But I don't have any gems!

162
00:05:42,458 --> 00:05:44,375
Then kiss rock!

163
00:05:44,375 --> 00:05:45,666
[gasping]

164
00:05:45,666 --> 00:05:47,291
[Kai] Leave my sister alone!

165
00:05:47,291 --> 00:05:49,041
[♪♪♪]

166
00:05:50,625 --> 00:05:51,625
Kai?

167
00:05:51,625 --> 00:05:53,083
What are you doing here?

168
00:05:53,083 --> 00:05:54,250
I came to help!

169
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:56,958
Sora and Wyldfyre
told me Jerk-face Jay bailed,

170
00:05:56,958 --> 00:05:58,333
and you're doing
a mission alone.

171
00:05:58,333 --> 00:05:59,958
Nice coconut.

172
00:05:59,958 --> 00:06:02,916
Not so bad yourself, handsome.

173
00:06:02,916 --> 00:06:05,625
[PowerLid] Gandy?

174
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:06,458
That you?

175
00:06:06,458 --> 00:06:07,708
Nope. Uh, uh...

176
00:06:07,708 --> 00:06:09,833
No, no, PowPow,

177
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:14,125
just a normal,
non-magical coconut.

178
00:06:14,125 --> 00:06:16,375
Stop lie, Gandy.

179
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:17,708
It been a while,

180
00:06:17,708 --> 00:06:22,666
but PowerLid recognize voice
of former BFF anywhere,

181
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:24,750
and it good to see you again,

182
00:06:24,750 --> 00:06:27,583
because now PowerLid
will get revenge!

183
00:06:30,333 --> 00:06:31,375
[roaring ferociously]

184
00:06:32,875 --> 00:06:33,875
[clattering outside]

185
00:06:33,875 --> 00:06:36,416
[clanking loudly]

186
00:06:38,208 --> 00:06:39,666
[tiptoes pattering,
low growling]

187
00:06:43,458 --> 00:06:45,166
[soft grunting]

188
00:06:45,166 --> 00:06:46,166
Shh! Keep it down!

189
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:47,666
[yelping and squeaking]

190
00:06:47,666 --> 00:06:49,166
[grunting]

191
00:06:49,166 --> 00:06:50,458
[clattering, gasping]

192
00:06:52,041 --> 00:06:53,083
[sighing]

193
00:06:54,916 --> 00:06:56,625
Phew!

194
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:02,500
Hey, seen a jeweled box
about yea big?

195
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,833
No, what's in it?

196
00:07:03,833 --> 00:07:06,416
A little something called
mind your own business.

197
00:07:06,416 --> 00:07:09,541
I'll show you my business!

198
00:07:09,541 --> 00:07:11,000
[grunting] Ah!

199
00:07:12,250 --> 00:07:14,625
What are you looking at, buddy?

200
00:07:17,083 --> 00:07:19,708
[gasping in delight]
My treasure!

201
00:07:19,708 --> 00:07:21,250
Shh!

202
00:07:22,708 --> 00:07:24,375
[roaring]

203
00:07:24,375 --> 00:07:27,000
Sorceress hurt
PowerLid's feelings,

204
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,458
so PowerLid will hurt
everyone's everything!

205
00:07:30,458 --> 00:07:31,583
[slamming]

206
00:07:31,583 --> 00:07:33,041
[crazed roaring]

207
00:07:33,041 --> 00:07:34,416
[Kai] Wait! PowerLid!

208
00:07:34,416 --> 00:07:36,791
I used to be just like you!

209
00:07:36,791 --> 00:07:39,041
Then you got second eye?

210
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:40,125
What? No.

211
00:07:40,125 --> 00:07:42,916
No, I mean,
it used to be easier for me

212
00:07:42,916 --> 00:07:44,333
to confront my enemies

213
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:45,791
than my feelings,

214
00:07:45,791 --> 00:07:47,041
but I learned this--

215
00:07:47,041 --> 00:07:49,041
lashing out dulls emotions,

216
00:07:49,041 --> 00:07:50,583
but not for long.

217
00:07:50,583 --> 00:07:53,250
Those bad feelings
come back worse than ever.

218
00:07:53,250 --> 00:07:54,958
Then what solution?

219
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:56,041
Bash rocks?

220
00:07:56,041 --> 00:07:57,000
[chuckling]

221
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,458
I wish it were that easy,

222
00:07:58,458 --> 00:07:59,750
but no,

223
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:02,041
it's... communication.

224
00:08:02,041 --> 00:08:04,291
[sighing heavily]

225
00:08:04,291 --> 00:08:05,291
Gandy?

226
00:08:05,291 --> 00:08:07,666
You were PowerLid's best friend,

227
00:08:07,666 --> 00:08:10,916
then one day you supposed
to come on gem hunt,

228
00:08:10,916 --> 00:08:12,333
never show up.

229
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:14,375
PowerLid try to find you.

230
00:08:14,375 --> 00:08:16,250
You just gone.

231
00:08:16,250 --> 00:08:18,291
You abandon PowerLid.

232
00:08:18,291 --> 00:08:19,833
Not good friend.

233
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:21,083
[sighing heavily]

234
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:24,416
It was supposed to be
an a capella vocal practice,

235
00:08:24,416 --> 00:08:27,916
but you scheduled a gem hunt
without asking.

236
00:08:27,916 --> 00:08:30,375
It became "gem this,"
"gem that."

237
00:08:30,375 --> 00:08:33,875
Gems crowded out
everything else in your brain.

238
00:08:33,875 --> 00:08:35,208
You changed!

239
00:08:35,208 --> 00:08:37,250
You change too!

240
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:38,916
You coconut now!

241
00:08:38,916 --> 00:08:41,583
This isn't me, you big dummy!

242
00:08:41,583 --> 00:08:44,708
This is my backup personality,

243
00:08:44,708 --> 00:08:47,583
but... you're right.

244
00:08:47,583 --> 00:08:49,625
I should have talked to you,

245
00:08:49,625 --> 00:08:52,166
not just disappeared.

246
00:08:52,166 --> 00:08:55,000
Sorry, PowPow.

247
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,416
PowerLid sorry too, Gandy.

248
00:09:00,208 --> 00:09:01,250
Great.

249
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:03,750
Now, sorry
to cut this reunion short,

250
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:05,750
but we need to ring those bells.

251
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:08,750
No problem. You go.

252
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:10,875
Only cost six gems.

253
00:09:10,875 --> 00:09:12,125
Friends discount.

254
00:09:12,125 --> 00:09:14,125
But-but she apologized.

255
00:09:14,125 --> 00:09:15,666
You made up!

256
00:09:15,666 --> 00:09:17,166
Yes, nice,

257
00:09:17,166 --> 00:09:18,375
but unrelated issue.

258
00:09:18,375 --> 00:09:20,708
PowerLid,
you can't focus on us.

259
00:09:20,708 --> 00:09:22,666
You've got to gather up
your gems!

260
00:09:22,666 --> 00:09:24,250
What Red talk about?

261
00:09:24,250 --> 00:09:25,541
My gems all safe

262
00:09:25,541 --> 00:09:27,208
in nice crate right over--

263
00:09:28,625 --> 00:09:31,000
Aah! My gems!

264
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
PowerLid coming for you!

265
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Make you safe!

266
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,166
Run now. Run!
Run, run, run!

267
00:09:35,166 --> 00:09:37,666
[PowerLid panting in distress]

268
00:09:38,791 --> 00:09:42,458
[cackling] Rapton stays winning!

269
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:45,458
[quietly]
We can't let them get away.

270
00:09:45,458 --> 00:09:47,375
Arrakore trusted us
to guard his treasure

271
00:09:47,375 --> 00:09:48,875
while he creates the Arc Dragon.

272
00:09:48,875 --> 00:09:51,291
He did? I don't
remember him saying that.

273
00:09:51,291 --> 00:09:52,458
It was implied.

274
00:09:53,208 --> 00:09:54,875
[mechanisms clicking]

275
00:09:56,041 --> 00:09:59,666
Be sure to thank
the angry Djinn for Rapton

276
00:09:59,666 --> 00:10:01,916
when he wakes up! Ha ha!

277
00:10:01,916 --> 00:10:03,500
[quietly] We can't
let the bombs explode

278
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:04,875
and distract Arrakore!

279
00:10:04,875 --> 00:10:06,125
[whispering] Obviously.

280
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:10,375
[roaring]

281
00:10:14,083 --> 00:10:15,916
[exploding]

282
00:10:18,708 --> 00:10:20,541
Phew!

283
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:24,000
[novelty car horn blaring]

284
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,291
Should we go after them?

285
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,291
No, we should wait
for Arrakore.

286
00:10:27,291 --> 00:10:30,166
Your wait is over.

287
00:10:30,166 --> 00:10:31,291
Did you do it?

288
00:10:31,291 --> 00:10:33,000
Go see for yourself.

289
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,166
[growling roar]

290
00:10:34,166 --> 00:10:37,416
Meanwhile, I'm going to sleep
for a week.

291
00:10:39,375 --> 00:10:40,500
[groaning sleepily]

292
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,916
Well, what are we waiting for?

293
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:50,208
[Lloyd] We're getting close.

294
00:10:50,208 --> 00:10:52,708
We should head down
before ThunderFang spots us.

295
00:10:58,291 --> 00:11:00,083
[thudding heavily]

296
00:11:01,291 --> 00:11:02,916
[Arin] The Well should be
right up there--

297
00:11:02,916 --> 00:11:04,583
[deafening clang]

298
00:11:06,250 --> 00:11:08,750
ThunderFang's
all over that Well

299
00:11:08,750 --> 00:11:11,458
like a lattice crust
on a snowberry pie.

300
00:11:11,458 --> 00:11:13,000
How are we supposed to get
the Unbidden Storm

301
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,083
down in there?

302
00:11:15,666 --> 00:11:17,958
Even if we find a way
to distract him long enough,

303
00:11:17,958 --> 00:11:20,166
he must have this place
heavily guarded.

304
00:11:20,166 --> 00:11:22,541
[Arin] Like, by them?

305
00:11:22,541 --> 00:11:23,541
[unearthly screeching]

306
00:11:27,083 --> 00:11:28,958
[screeching]

307
00:11:30,208 --> 00:11:31,666
H'yah!

308
00:11:31,666 --> 00:11:33,083
Ha! H'yah!

309
00:11:33,083 --> 00:11:34,250
[laughing] All right!

310
00:11:34,250 --> 00:11:35,791
Prismatic armor works!

311
00:11:35,791 --> 00:11:37,333
Remind me to thank Sora.

312
00:11:37,333 --> 00:11:38,833
[Arin] If we get the chance.

313
00:11:42,791 --> 00:11:43,916
Be brave like the ninja,

314
00:11:43,916 --> 00:11:45,166
brave like the ninja...

315
00:11:45,166 --> 00:11:49,250
I, Alfonzo Elias Frohicky,

316
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:52,458
Assistant Keeper
of the Monastery,

317
00:11:52,458 --> 00:11:54,750
will not permit you to--

318
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,500
Permit me?

319
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:58,333
My strength permits me.

320
00:12:02,083 --> 00:12:03,375
[wailing]

321
00:12:03,375 --> 00:12:04,458
Haah!

322
00:12:04,458 --> 00:12:05,791
[grunting with impact]

323
00:12:05,791 --> 00:12:07,875
[groaning]

324
00:12:11,791 --> 00:12:14,208
My family is in this Monastery,

325
00:12:14,208 --> 00:12:16,291
and I'll defend them
to my last breath.

326
00:12:16,291 --> 00:12:17,916
So not for long, then.

327
00:12:18,875 --> 00:12:19,791
[growling]

328
00:12:21,375 --> 00:12:22,750
Aah!

329
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:28,666
H'yah!

330
00:12:30,666 --> 00:12:32,083
Haah!

331
00:12:36,416 --> 00:12:40,125
[groaning]

332
00:12:40,125 --> 00:12:41,708
Go!

333
00:12:41,708 --> 00:12:43,208
Hide!

334
00:12:46,416 --> 00:12:47,916
[growling]

335
00:12:47,916 --> 00:12:50,875
I don't need a weapon
to destroy you.

336
00:12:51,875 --> 00:12:55,708
I can defeat you
with my bare hands.

337
00:13:03,083 --> 00:13:05,083
You are just as lost

338
00:13:05,083 --> 00:13:08,041
as those children
you fail to protect!

339
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:13,666
H'yah!

340
00:13:13,666 --> 00:13:15,166
[grunting with impact]

341
00:13:18,291 --> 00:13:20,750
[groaning]

342
00:13:30,958 --> 00:13:34,166
You will take me to Wu's--

343
00:13:34,166 --> 00:13:36,583
What is so amusing?

344
00:13:36,583 --> 00:13:39,375
Something's
coming from the east.

345
00:13:40,583 --> 00:13:41,750
[grunting]

346
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,041
I once trapped a Source Dragon.

347
00:13:48,041 --> 00:13:49,708
Am I to tremble

348
00:13:49,708 --> 00:13:51,916
in front of a decrepit
old lizard

349
00:13:51,916 --> 00:13:53,333
on her last legs?

350
00:13:53,333 --> 00:13:56,833
A Tiger Tribe warrior
without honor?

351
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:58,791
Zarkar himself would be ashamed

352
00:13:58,791 --> 00:14:01,708
to find his last descendant
sunk to--

353
00:14:01,708 --> 00:14:03,916
[gasping]
A Source Dragon Icon?

354
00:14:05,625 --> 00:14:08,750
Two icons? Impossible.

355
00:14:10,708 --> 00:14:13,583
Send my greetings to Egalt.

356
00:14:13,583 --> 00:14:15,083
H'yah!

357
00:14:18,875 --> 00:14:20,541
[roaring in pain]

358
00:14:22,166 --> 00:14:24,041
Hi-yah!

359
00:14:25,583 --> 00:14:26,541
[groaning with impact]

360
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:32,000
Aah!

361
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Now, show me to Wu's study.

362
00:14:39,416 --> 00:14:40,583
[cackling]

363
00:14:40,583 --> 00:14:43,291
Rapton would risk
a thousand henchmen's lives

364
00:14:43,291 --> 00:14:44,291
for you,

365
00:14:44,291 --> 00:14:47,125
the greatest treasure of all,

366
00:14:47,125 --> 00:14:50,666
a rare Djinjagan variant.

367
00:14:50,666 --> 00:14:53,666
My collection
is finally complete.

368
00:14:53,666 --> 00:14:55,000
Incoming!

369
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,250
[unearthly shrieking]

370
00:14:57,791 --> 00:14:59,458
Aah!

371
00:14:59,458 --> 00:15:00,583
Whew!

372
00:15:00,583 --> 00:15:03,083
I'd sure hate to be
whoever she's after.

373
00:15:15,916 --> 00:15:17,083
[unearthly shrieking]

374
00:15:17,791 --> 00:15:19,041
Spectral armor or not,

375
00:15:19,041 --> 00:15:21,000
I don't know how much longer
these mechs can hold up.

376
00:15:27,166 --> 00:15:28,708
Whoo whoo!

377
00:15:29,583 --> 00:15:30,750
Whoa! [grunting with effort]

378
00:15:32,958 --> 00:15:34,791
[slamming]

379
00:15:35,958 --> 00:15:37,166
I'll hold them off!

380
00:15:37,166 --> 00:15:38,291
Get down that well!

381
00:15:41,458 --> 00:15:42,833
How?

382
00:15:44,125 --> 00:15:45,125
Wait...

383
00:15:45,125 --> 00:15:46,291
Bleckt said
there's a whole cavern

384
00:15:46,291 --> 00:15:47,500
beneath the Well, right?

385
00:15:50,291 --> 00:15:51,166
[unearthly shrieking]

386
00:15:52,125 --> 00:15:53,000
H'yah!

387
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,041
[slamming]

388
00:15:55,291 --> 00:15:56,708
-[unearthly shrieking]
-Help me!

389
00:15:58,875 --> 00:16:01,416
You sure
this is the best ide--?

390
00:16:01,958 --> 00:16:03,625
[unearthly shrieking]

391
00:16:03,625 --> 00:16:05,458
[slamming]

392
00:16:05,458 --> 00:16:06,333
[unearthly shrieking]

393
00:16:07,666 --> 00:16:09,291
[unearthly shrieking]

394
00:16:12,166 --> 00:16:13,625
-[rock crumbling]
-Wha...!

395
00:16:16,666 --> 00:16:19,583
Arrakore and Zanth,
they did it!

396
00:16:19,583 --> 00:16:20,541
[gasping] Look!

397
00:16:22,375 --> 00:16:24,166
Okay.

398
00:16:24,166 --> 00:16:26,916
Song-spell time.

399
00:16:26,916 --> 00:16:28,750
Slow your roll, Mr. Eager.

400
00:16:28,750 --> 00:16:31,416
Let's rehearse
and get this right.

401
00:16:31,416 --> 00:16:33,625
♪ Hmm-hmm-hmm... ♪

402
00:16:33,625 --> 00:16:35,791
♪ Da-da-da... ♪

403
00:16:35,791 --> 00:16:39,458
♪ La-da-da
La-da-da-da... ♪

404
00:16:39,458 --> 00:16:41,000
-That's not right!
-You're messing it up!

405
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,166
[Wyldfyre] You're both wrong!

406
00:16:42,166 --> 00:16:45,416
It was [singing "La Cucaracha"]

407
00:16:45,416 --> 00:16:47,125
[together]
That was Rapton's horn!

408
00:16:48,166 --> 00:16:49,166
Oh, right.

409
00:16:49,166 --> 00:16:50,291
Oh, no.

410
00:16:50,291 --> 00:16:53,916
In all the chaos,
we've forgotten the song!

411
00:16:58,958 --> 00:17:02,208
[humming spell song]

412
00:17:02,208 --> 00:17:05,541
That's a Spell Song of Waking,
all right.

413
00:17:05,541 --> 00:17:07,375
Very powerful magic.

414
00:17:07,375 --> 00:17:10,208
Uh... one small problem.

415
00:17:13,208 --> 00:17:15,000
Where are the bells?

416
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,416
Uh, bummer.

417
00:17:16,416 --> 00:17:18,958
The bells have been
in Mysterium so long,

418
00:17:18,958 --> 00:17:20,833
the natural magic of the land

419
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:22,458
must have transfigured them.

420
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:23,916
Meh, it happens.

421
00:17:23,916 --> 00:17:26,166
Bells into doves,
purses into piglets,

422
00:17:26,166 --> 00:17:28,291
shopping bags into
wandering theater troupes.

423
00:17:28,291 --> 00:17:30,666
How are we supposed
to ring a dove?

424
00:17:30,666 --> 00:17:33,791
[humming a melody]

425
00:17:33,791 --> 00:17:37,416
[humming
competing melodies]

426
00:17:37,416 --> 00:17:39,666
[grumbling a melody]

427
00:17:39,666 --> 00:17:41,875
We can't keep going
back and forth.

428
00:17:41,875 --> 00:17:43,250
We're running out of time!

429
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:44,666
You don't know the melody.

430
00:17:44,666 --> 00:17:46,208
You weren't even there, Frak.

431
00:17:46,208 --> 00:17:47,958
I listened
the first time you taught me.

432
00:17:47,958 --> 00:17:51,375
I have perfect pitch?

433
00:17:54,416 --> 00:17:55,250
[bell chiming]

434
00:17:59,583 --> 00:18:01,458
[bell chiming]

435
00:18:01,458 --> 00:18:02,500
[error tone buzzing]

436
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:05,083
[Sora] Looks like we only have
three chances...

437
00:18:05,083 --> 00:18:07,583
and we've already wasted one.

438
00:18:09,041 --> 00:18:10,666
[squawking]

439
00:18:11,791 --> 00:18:13,291
[yelping] Aah!

440
00:18:13,291 --> 00:18:14,291
[spluttering]

441
00:18:14,291 --> 00:18:16,166
I never thought I'd say this,

442
00:18:16,166 --> 00:18:18,750
but I wish Fugi-Dove were here.

443
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:20,250
Doves are the worst.

444
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:22,041
No self-respecting spellcaster

445
00:18:22,041 --> 00:18:23,750
would have one as a familiar.

446
00:18:23,750 --> 00:18:25,791
Now, Janet had a dove.

447
00:18:25,791 --> 00:18:28,375
Trained it to befoul
my cauldron whenever I--

448
00:18:28,375 --> 00:18:31,625
Wait, you say this Janet
trained her dove?

449
00:18:31,625 --> 00:18:32,750
How?

450
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:33,750
Snacks.

451
00:18:33,750 --> 00:18:35,791
All simple-minded creatures

452
00:18:35,791 --> 00:18:37,541
are motivated by food.

453
00:18:37,541 --> 00:18:39,708
[grumbling]
Oh, don't mention food.

454
00:18:39,708 --> 00:18:41,208
I'm so hungry!

455
00:18:41,208 --> 00:18:44,541
I could actually eat
these gross wafers Geo made.

456
00:18:44,541 --> 00:18:47,000
[whimpering and munching]

457
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,750
[gagging] Ugh, never mind.
No, I'm not.

458
00:18:48,750 --> 00:18:50,500
You have snacks?

459
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:51,458
Gimme those!

460
00:18:57,250 --> 00:18:58,375
Come on...

461
00:18:58,375 --> 00:19:00,041
Polly want a... this thing?

462
00:19:00,041 --> 00:19:01,041
[dove cooing]

463
00:19:01,750 --> 00:19:04,125
Come on, birdy, we need this!

464
00:19:06,625 --> 00:19:08,833
[chirping a note]

465
00:19:08,833 --> 00:19:10,541
It worked!

466
00:19:11,583 --> 00:19:14,375
-[bell chiming]
-You got this!

467
00:19:14,375 --> 00:19:16,000
Dominate those bells!

468
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,375
Raar!

469
00:19:17,375 --> 00:19:19,583
[bells chiming]

470
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:24,833
[humming melody]

471
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:26,750
By all means, take your time.

472
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:28,541
Not like the world
is going to end!

473
00:19:28,541 --> 00:19:30,833
[humming melody]

474
00:19:30,833 --> 00:19:33,416
[bell chiming]

475
00:19:33,416 --> 00:19:35,000
[error tone buzzing]

476
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,083
[Frak sighs]

477
00:19:36,083 --> 00:19:37,375
One chance left.

478
00:19:39,083 --> 00:19:40,208
I'll take it from here.

479
00:19:40,208 --> 00:19:41,250
I can do it!

480
00:19:41,250 --> 00:19:42,958
I only made one mistake.

481
00:19:42,958 --> 00:19:45,083
Which I watched
and learned from.

482
00:19:45,083 --> 00:19:47,041
Nope. You've each gone already.

483
00:19:47,041 --> 00:19:48,041
My turn!

484
00:19:51,083 --> 00:19:52,000
-Stop!
-Stop!

485
00:19:53,833 --> 00:19:54,791
[chirping note]

486
00:19:54,791 --> 00:19:55,791
[bell chiming]

487
00:19:55,791 --> 00:19:57,208
[chirping note]

488
00:19:57,208 --> 00:19:58,333
[bell chiming]

489
00:19:58,333 --> 00:19:59,250
[chirping note]

490
00:19:59,250 --> 00:20:00,416
[bell chiming]

491
00:20:00,416 --> 00:20:02,208
-[chirping note]
-[bell chiming]

492
00:20:02,208 --> 00:20:03,916
[chirping, chiming]

493
00:20:03,916 --> 00:20:05,458
[chirping and chiming notes]

494
00:20:05,458 --> 00:20:08,416
[tone reverberating]

495
00:20:08,416 --> 00:20:12,791
[bells tolling waking spell]

496
00:20:12,791 --> 00:20:15,666
[♪♪♪]

497
00:20:17,666 --> 00:20:19,458
[growling]

498
00:20:19,458 --> 00:20:21,083
[roaring]

499
00:20:26,625 --> 00:20:29,666
[roaring]

500
00:20:34,708 --> 00:20:36,625
[roaring]

501
00:20:39,166 --> 00:20:40,416
Did it work?

502
00:20:40,416 --> 00:20:41,666
Maybe?

503
00:20:41,666 --> 00:20:44,208
Let's hope everyone else
is doing their part now.

504
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:47,083
[stones crumbling]

505
00:20:47,083 --> 00:20:48,250
[Lloyd grunts with effort]

506
00:20:48,250 --> 00:20:50,166
[coughing]

507
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:51,875
Arin!

508
00:20:51,875 --> 00:20:54,291
[Arin] I'm okay!

509
00:20:56,333 --> 00:20:58,958
Arin, I'm sorry.

510
00:20:58,958 --> 00:21:01,541
I was so focused on
getting us down here,

511
00:21:01,541 --> 00:21:03,875
I didn't think about
the consequences.

512
00:21:03,875 --> 00:21:05,958
I'm fine, and look!

513
00:21:05,958 --> 00:21:06,916
[Lloyd] Is that... ?

514
00:21:06,916 --> 00:21:08,416
[Arin] Let's find out.

515
00:21:11,708 --> 00:21:13,833
We're below
the Well of the Lost!

516
00:21:13,833 --> 00:21:14,875
You did it!

517
00:21:14,875 --> 00:21:16,208
Now we just need...

518
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:17,833
The Unbidden Storm!

519
00:21:17,833 --> 00:21:20,750
I must have dropped it
in the fall!

520
00:21:27,708 --> 00:21:30,333
[Lloyd]
It broke during the cave-in.

521
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:33,708
I ruined our last chance
to stop ThunderFang.

522
00:21:41,875 --> 00:21:42,791
[cackling malevolently]

523
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,875
[♪♪♪]

